-- REFUSED: `Regulative` (Blocking).
-- The exported decision's body is a regulative rule (PARTY/MUST/WITHIN/
-- HENCE/LEST). Docassemble has no deontic runtime in v1 (spec §5, §11):
-- the lowering must refuse the `Regulative{}` constructor by name and
-- record a Blocking FidelityNote — never emit an interview that silently
-- drops the obligation.
-- The file itself typechecks: the refusal belongs to `l4 docassemble`.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Landlord, Tenant

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `serve notice`
    `vacate premises`

@export The landlord's obligation to serve notice before seeking possession
GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the landlord has to serve notice
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
DECIDE `notice obligation` IS
    PARTY Landlord
    MUST  `serve notice`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY Landlord BECAUSE "possession sought without notice"
